msgid "Connecting to the Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-airbotpower-power-module.rst:70
#: 6e3e30c14cbd493589f3c18ce152e01e
msgid "Connecting the main power supply, backup power supply and servo rail \"safety\" connector, are shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-airbotpower-power-module.rst:78
#: a4d65d72477a4696aa583ce511870d3d
msgid "A few practical guidelines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-airbotpower-power-module.rst:80
#: 6d47574632b0475883a2be2a2519161d
msgid "Don't use servos on the backup AUX 5.3V supply as they can supply just a few amps and too many servos might exceed this amperage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-airbotpower-power-module.rst:82
#: 1a5aec146df749d8892cf195ebcf11fa
msgid "At least one of the DIP switch switches MUST be switched ON towards the ON mark (or towards the battery number marks); In the first batch of boards, DIP switches labels have been printed in reverse order: 3S, 4S,...,7S, 8S should instead be read reversely 8S, 7S? ...4S, 3S. Later batches will have their labels printed in the correct order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-airbotpower-power-module.rst:87
#: f8c35f10dc9a4db39e4e35cedd4e95ae
msgid "On the bottom of the Power Board, there are some gold plated traces between the sensor and the 7mm holes and between BAT- and the PDB- . It is advised to add some solder on them for extreme currents. To do this you'll need at least a 80W soldering iron and must use good solder with 2-2.5% non-corrosive flux. Higher power soldering iron leads to shorter heating time which is better for both the PCB itself and the components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-airbotpower-power-module.rst:95
#: 7d912d9204354b9cb737cf429b5ff390
msgid "The board also comes with a Zener Diode 5.6V (5W) + capacitor and easy instructions to assemble them into an extra safety module that plugs on the autopilot’s servo rail. This is required on the autopilot's servo rail to trim any short voltage spikes (above 5.6V) that would be fed back to the autopilot''s servo rail from external devices & servos (possibly causing the autopilot to shut itself down)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-airbotpower-power-module.rst:105
#: e074870467594f36be697f11690465d4
msgid "5.6V 5WZener+Cap module details: plastidip & heat shrink tubing"
msgstr ""

